               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, a 36-year-old male admitted on 30/03/2008 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever. Clinical examination revealed marked tenderness at McBurney's point with rebound tenderness. Laboratory findings demonstrated leukocytosis, and abdominal ultrasound confirmed appendiceal inflammation consistent with acute appendicitis. The patient underwent an uncomplicated laparoscopic appendectomy on 31/03/2008. Histopathological examination confirmed acute appendicitis without perforation. Postoperative recovery was uneventful, with adequate pain control achieved using standard analgesics. The patient was mobilised early and tolerated oral intake well. He was discharged on 02/04/2008 in good general condition. Please arrange follow-up in approximately two weeks for wound inspection and review of histology results. Should any concerns arise, please do not hesitate to contact us.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
